fix: close the export-mode boundaries, the fork cut and the retry safety hole

Review-driven, v0.5.1. No new features. The two structural claims still hold —
the Session log is the only source of truth, and every edit/delete is a fork, so
the original conversation is never touched.

Failure first: ten tests were written against e331baf and all ten failed before
any fix, covering each defect below.

1. Export-mode boundaries.

   `standard` and `brief` were still emitting `compaction/summary`, which stands
   in for history the user never wrote, and the default header still carried the
   workspace path and the parent Session id. Both are now written only by `full`,
   the mode that already warns about local paths. Every mode still says, in its
   own header, that the user's messages are included verbatim and may contain
   secrets — the narrower modes only remove what the agent added.

2. resolveMode could widen instead of narrow.

   `reasoning=false&tools=true` resolved to `full`, so it gained the thinking it
   had just excluded; `reasoning=true&tools=false` gained the tool payloads it
   had excluded; and `mode=<illegal>` fell through to the legacy branch, where
   `reasoning=true` upgraded it to `full`. The mode now sets a ceiling and the
   legacy switches may only lower it — `true` is a permission, never a demand —
   and an unrecognised mode falls back to `standard` and stays there.

3. Regenerate forked at the wrong seq.

   `onRegenerate` cut at `dropSeq`, which keeps the turn's own `user/message`,
   and then submitted that same text again: the child carried the user's message
   twice. Every branch action now goes through one `branchPlan`, which always
   cuts at `cutSeq` — before the turn — so the resend is the only copy.

   The v0.5.0 automatic retry is removed. `inputActions.submit()` carries no
   idempotency guarantee, so a rejected call may already have delivered the
   message and a second automatic call could send it twice. A rejection now parks
   the payload in `failed`, `resendNextState` never leaves that state on its own,
   and a small bar above the composer offers **Send again** and **Dismiss** while
   the text stays in the draft.

4. Prefetching was too eager.

   Opening the menu mounted three rows that each prefetched their own mode, so
   the menu fetched three documents including the full record. Only the default
   mode is prefetched now, concurrent requests for one Session+mode share a
   single fetch, the cache expires after 5s instead of 30s, and `invalidate()`
   drops a Session's cached and in-flight exports when the conversation moves on.

5. CI.

   `npm run check` syntax-checks every source file and runs the suite; GitHub
   Actions runs it on ubuntu-latest and windows-latest and prints the counts as
   one explicit line (tests=66 pass=66 fail=0 skipped=0).

The test harness grew a real hook runtime, a clock seam and a timer recorder, so
the behaviour-only components and the cache are testable without a browser.
Recording timers also removed a 30s stall: the suite runs in ~2.4s instead of 30.

66 tests, 0 skipped. Verified live against the running Harness on a 2.6 MB
conversation: standard returned 268,630 chars with no workspace path in its
header and zero compaction headings; full returned 2,671,526 chars with both.
